{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "genotyping",
  "_why_schema_version": "Mandatory. With {frz}/{new} expansion, @-over-callers and a second module in flight, a reader must be able to tell a stale reader from a stale file. A version this build does not implement is a refusal, never a best-effort parse.",
  "callers": [
    "manta",
    "wham",
    "scramble"
  ],
  "_why_callers": "dragen/melt produced nothing in this cohort. The list is bound, not commented out: GenerateBatchMetrics.wdl feeds dragen_vcf/melt_vcf through select_all([...]), so omitting them changes the merged VCF count, and `check` reports them as upstream-only on steps 06/07/08 rather than as unknown keys.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": "06-GenerateBatchMetrics",
      "wdl": "GenerateBatchMetrics",
      "workflow": "GenerateBatchMetrics",
      "rootEntityType": "sample_set",
      "inputs": {
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.batch": "this.sample_set_id",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.pe_file": "this.merged_PE{frz}",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.sr_file": "this.merged_SR{frz}",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.baf_file": "this.merged_BAF{frz}",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.rd_file": "this.merged_bincov{frz}",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.median_file": "this.median_cov{frz}",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.ped_file": "workspace.cohort_ped_file",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.depth_vcf": "this.clustered_depth_vcf{frz}",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.@_vcf": "this.clustered_@_vcf{frz}",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.primary_contigs_list": "workspace.primary_contigs_list",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.chr_x": "workspace.chr_x",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.chr_y": "workspace.chr_y",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.rmsk": "workspace.rmsk",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.segdups": "workspace.segdups",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.reference_dict": "workspace.reference_dict",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.gatk_docker": "workspace.gatk_docker",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.sv_pipeline_docker": "workspace.sv_pipeline_docker",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.sv_base_mini_docker": "workspace.sv_base_mini_docker"
      },
      "outputs": {
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.metrics": "this.metrics{new}",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.metrics_file_batchmetrics": "this.metrics_file_batchmetrics{new}",
        "GenerateBatchMetrics.ploidy_table": "this.ploidy_table{new}"
      }
    },
    {
      "step": "07-FilterBatchSites",
      "wdl": "FilterBatchSites",
      "workflow": "FilterBatchSites",
      "rootEntityType": "sample_set",
      "inputs": {
        "FilterBatchSites.batch": "this.sample_set_id",
        "FilterBatchSites.evidence_metrics": "this.metrics{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.depth_vcf": "this.clustered_depth_vcf{frz}",
        "FilterBatchSites.@_vcf": "this.clustered_@_vcf{frz}",
        "FilterBatchSites.sv_pipeline_docker": "workspace.sv_pipeline_docker",
        "FilterBatchSites.N_IQR_cutoff_plotting": "6"
      },
      "_why_FilterBatchSites.N_IQR_cutoff_plotting": "the value is the STRING \"6\" (and step 08's \"10000\"), because that is what this map has always posted and what Rawls accepted. Rule 3 says a literal carries its real type; the type recorded here is the one on the wire. Changing it to a JSON number changes the bytes of the POST, so it is not a refactor and does not belong in this file.",
      "outputs": {
        "FilterBatchSites.sites_filtered_depth_vcf": "this.sites_filtered_depth_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.sites_filtered_manta_vcf": "this.sites_filtered_manta_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.sites_filtered_scramble_vcf": "this.sites_filtered_scramble_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.sites_filtered_wham_vcf": "this.sites_filtered_wham_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.cutoffs": "this.cutoffs{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.scores": "this.scores{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.RF_intermediate_files": "this.RF_intermediate_files{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.sites_filtered_sv_counts": "this.sites_filtered_sv_counts{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.sites_filtered_sv_count_plots": "this.sites_filtered_sv_count_plots{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.sites_filtered_outlier_samples_preview": "this.sites_filtered_outlier_samples_preview{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.sites_filtered_outlier_samples_with_reason": "this.sites_filtered_outlier_samples_with_reason{new}",
        "FilterBatchSites.sites_filtered_num_outlier_samples": "this.sites_filtered_num_outlier_samples{new}"
      }
    },
    {
      "step": "08-FilterBatchSamples",
      "wdl": "FilterBatchSamples",
      "workflow": "FilterBatchSamples",
      "rootEntityType": "sample_set",
      "inputs": {
        "FilterBatchSamples.batch": "this.sample_set_id",
        "FilterBatchSamples.N_IQR_cutoff": "10000",
        "FilterBatchSamples.depth_vcf": "this.sites_filtered_depth_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.@_vcf": "this.sites_filtered_@_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.sv_pipeline_docker": "workspace.sv_pipeline_docker",
        "FilterBatchSamples.sv_base_mini_docker": "workspace.sv_base_mini_docker",
        "FilterBatchSamples.linux_docker": "workspace.linux_docker"
      },
      "_why_FilterBatchSamples.N_IQR_cutoff": "the value is the STRING \"6\" (and step 08's \"10000\"), because that is what this map has always posted and what Rawls accepted. Rule 3 says a literal carries its real type; the type recorded here is the one on the wire. Changing it to a JSON number changes the bytes of the POST, so it is not a refactor and does not belong in this file.",
      "outputs": {
        "FilterBatchSamples.outlier_filtered_depth_vcf": "this.outlier_filtered_depth_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.outlier_filtered_depth_vcf_index": "this.outlier_filtered_depth_vcf_index{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.outlier_filtered_manta_vcf": "this.outlier_filtered_manta_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.outlier_filtered_scramble_vcf": "this.outlier_filtered_scramble_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.outlier_filtered_wham_vcf": "this.outlier_filtered_wham_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.outlier_filtered_pesr_vcf": "this.outlier_filtered_pesr_vcf{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.outlier_filtered_pesr_vcf_index": "this.outlier_filtered_pesr_vcf_index{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.filtered_batch_samples_file": "this.filtered_batch_samples_file{new}",
        "FilterBatchSamples.outlier_samples_excluded_file": "this.outlier_samples_excluded_file{new}"
      }
    },
    {
      "step": "09-MergeBatchSites",
      "wdl": "MergeBatchSites",
      "workflow": "MergeBatchSites",
      "rootEntityType": "sample_set_set",
      "inputs": {
        "MergeBatchSites.cohort": "this.sample_set_set_id",
        "MergeBatchSites.pesr_vcfs": "this.sample_sets.outlier_filtered_pesr_vcf{new}",
        "MergeBatchSites.depth_vcfs": "this.sample_sets.outlier_filtered_depth_vcf{new}",
        "MergeBatchSites.ploidy_tables": "this.sample_sets.ploidy_table{new}",
        "MergeBatchSites.reference_fasta": "workspace.reference_fasta",
        "MergeBatchSites.reference_fasta_fai": "workspace.reference_index",
        "MergeBatchSites.reference_dict": "workspace.reference_dict",
        "MergeBatchSites.sv_base_mini_docker": "workspace.sv_base_mini_docker",
        "MergeBatchSites.sv_pipeline_docker": "workspace.sv_pipeline_docker",
        "MergeBatchSites.gatk_docker": "workspace.gatk_docker"
      },
      "outputs": {
        "MergeBatchSites.merge_batch_sites_vcf": "workspace.merge_batch_sites_vcf{new}",
        "MergeBatchSites.merge_batch_sites_vcf_index": "workspace.merge_batch_sites_vcf_index{new}"
      }
    },
    {
      "step": "10-GenotypeBatch",
      "wdl": "GenotypeBatch",
      "workflow": "GenotypeBatch",
      "rootEntityType": "sample_set",
      "inputs": {
        "GenotypeBatch.batch": "this.sample_set_id",
        "GenotypeBatch.vcf": "workspace.merge_batch_sites_vcf{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.training_vcf": "this.outlier_filtered_pesr_vcf{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.rf_cutoffs": "this.cutoffs{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.median_coverage": "this.median_cov{frz}",
        "GenotypeBatch.rd_file": "this.merged_bincov{frz}",
        "GenotypeBatch.pe_file": "this.merged_PE{frz}",
        "GenotypeBatch.sr_file": "this.merged_SR{frz}",
        "GenotypeBatch.reference_dict": "workspace.reference_dict",
        "GenotypeBatch.training_intervals": "workspace.depth_training_bed",
        "GenotypeBatch.ploidy_table": "this.ploidy_table{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.depth_exclusion_intervals": "workspace.bin_exclude",
        "GenotypeBatch.pesr_exclusion_intervals": "workspace.pesr_exclude_list",
        "GenotypeBatch.contig_list": "workspace.primary_contigs_list",
        "GenotypeBatch.gatk_docker": "workspace.gatk_docker",
        "GenotypeBatch.sv_base_mini_docker": "workspace.sv_base_mini_docker",
        "GenotypeBatch.sv_pipeline_docker": "workspace.sv_pipeline_docker"
      },
      "branch_only_inputs": [
        "GenotypeBatch.training_vcf"
      ],
      "_why_GenotypeBatch.training_vcf": "branch-only: main trains PE/SR from `vcf`, the branch from a separate batch VCF. Both are coherent pipelines; they are different pipelines. Dropping it is a semantic change, not a fix. main's GenotypeBatch declares 21 inputs (18 + 3 dockers); the branch declares 26, adding training_vcf, genotype_args, training_args, n_RD_genotype_bins and fail_on_degenerate_sr_cutoffs. This map binds only training_vcf -- the other four have WDL defaults -- so it is the single key a main-shaped run has to drop. It was posted against a main-derived ref and rejected as an extra input; that is what happened, and this field is why `check` can name it instead of just failing.",
      "_why_unbound": "n_RD_genotype_bins (100000) and fail_on_degenerate_sr_cutoffs (true) come from the WDL defaults - the point of the branch is that these are now correct by default.",
      "outputs": {
        "GenotypeBatch.genotyped_depth_vcf": "this.genotyped_depth_vcf{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.genotyped_depth_vcf_index": "this.genotyped_depth_vcf_index{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.genotyped_pesr_vcf": "this.genotyped_pesr_vcf{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.genotyped_pesr_vcf_index": "this.genotyped_pesr_vcf_index{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.genotyping_rd_depth_table": "this.genotyping_rd_depth_table{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.genotyping_rd_pesr_table": "this.genotyping_rd_pesr_table{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.genotyping_pe_table": "this.genotyping_pe_table{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.genotyping_sr_table": "this.genotyping_sr_table{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.genotyping_sr_cutoff_diagnostics": "this.genotyping_sr_cutoff_diagnostics{new}",
        "GenotypeBatch.regeno_coverage_medians": "this.regeno_coverage_medians{new}"
      },
      "export": [
        "genotyped_pesr_vcf",
        "genotyped_depth_vcf",
        "genotyping_rd_depth_table",
        "genotyping_rd_pesr_table",
        "genotyping_pe_table",
        "genotyping_sr_table",
        "genotyping_sr_cutoff_diagnostics"
      ],
      "_why_export": "The new-side attributes terra/batch_fetch_compare.sh fetches off the entity once the chain finishes, as data rather than as shell literals (docs/gap-ledger.md A21; docs/module-profiles.md §9 step 4). These 7 are NOT derived from `outputs` and the loader deliberately does not compare the two: this step WRITES 10 attributes, 8 once §3 rule 4's `_index` siblings are excluded, and the script demanded 7 of those 8, carrying the eighth -- regeno_coverage_medians -- as optional. Promoting that eighth name was asked and REJECTED: `required` is the script's exit code, so a required attribute that some chain never wrote turns every such baseline into a fetch that exits 1 where it passes today -- a product decision with a money-path consequence, to be taken with a real run in hand, not smuggled inside a refactor. `scripts/selftest.d/profiles.sh`'s export-list guard pins these 7 against `outputs`, states the 7-vs-8 delta as a fact, and carries the positive control that edits THIS field to prove the shell follows the data rather than a literal."
    }
  ]
}
